ng 4) NINJA COURSE GRAND OPENING 5) DIRECTOR'S REPORT 6) ADJOURNMENT The next scheduled meeting will be held on Wednesday, January, 13th 2027 at 5:30 p.m. MST located at the Parks and Recreation Office at 296 East Murray Park Avenue, Murray, Utah. Special Accommodations for the hearing or visually impaired will be made upon a request to the office of Murray City Parks and Recreation (801-264-2614). We would appreciate notification two working days prior to the meeting. TTY is Relay Utah at #711. Committee members may participate in the meeting via telephonic communication. If a Committee member does participate via telephonic communication, the Committee member will be on speakerphone. The speakerphone will be amplified so that the other Committee members and all other persons present will be able to hear all discussions. At least 24 hours prior to the meeting, a copy of the foregoing notice was sent to the City Recorder to post in conspicuous view in the front foyer of the Murray City Center, Murray, Utah. A copy of this notice was also posted on Murray City's internet website www.murray.utah.gov and the state noticing website at http://pmn.utah.gov ","agendaPacketDocumentId":"DOC622S418","agendaPacketDocumentIds":["DOC622S418"],"agendaPacketEnabled":false,"agendaPostedDate":"2026-11-03T18:24:27.000Z","agendaSectionHeaderDescriptions":["<div>Those wishing to have their comments read into the record may send an email by 5:00 p.m. the day prior to the meeting date to kjones@murray.utah.gov. Comments are limited to three minutes or less (approximately 300 words for emails) and must include your name and address.</div>","<div>The next scheduled meeting will be held on <strong>Wednesday, ___________________, at 5:30 p.m. MST located at the Parks and Recreation Office at 296 East Murray Park Avenue, Murray, Utah. </strong><br><br>Special Accommodations for the hearing or visually impaired will be made upon a request to the office of Murray City Parks and Recreation (801-264-2614). We would appreciate notification two working days prior to the meeting. TTY is Relay Utah at #711.<br><br>Committee members may participate in the meeting via telephonic communication. If a Committee member does participate via telephonic communication, the Committee member will be on speakerphone. The speakerphone will be amplified so that the other Committee members and all other persons present will be able to hear all discussions.<br><br>At least 24 hours prior to the meeting, a copy of the foregoing notice was sent to the City Recorder to post in conspicuous view in the front foyer of the Murray City Center, Murray, Utah. A copy of this notice was also posted on Murray City's internet website www.murray.utah.gov and the state noticing website at <a href=\"http://pmn.utah.gov/\">http://pmn.utah.gov</a>.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div>"],"agendaSectionHeaderTitles":["CALL MEETING TO ORDER","APPROVAL OF MINUTES","SPECIAL RECOGNITION","CITIZEN COMMENT(S)","BUSINESS ITEM(S)","REPORT(S)","ANNOUNCEMENTS AND QUESTIONS","ADJOURNMENT","END OF MEETING"],"agendaSnippet":null,"agendaStatus":5,"agendaSummaryDocumentId":"","agendaSummaryDocumentIds":[],"agendaTitle":"Parks and Recreation Advisory Board 11/04/2026","base64ThumbnailsString":"","canceled":false,"description":"Parks and Recreation Advisory Board","endDateTime":"2026-11-04T06:00:00.000Z","endTime":"07:00 PM","id":"lb1roqEBxMNYVAgaRz_K","importAgenda":true,"importMinutes":false,"isPublicVisibility":1,"location":"296 E. Murray Park Ave","locationUploadUrl":"","meetingAgendaId":11173,"meetingId":447,"meetingTitle":"Parks and Recreation Advisory Board","meetingTypeBackgroundColor":"#b2dfdb","meetingTypeColor":"#009688","meetingTypeId":10,"meetingTypeName":"Parks and Recreation Advisory Board","minutesBase64ThumbNails":"","minutesId":0,"minutesMeetingAttachmentTitles":null,"minutesMeetingTitle":null,"minutesNotes":null,"minutesOCRedContent":"","minutesPacketDocumentId":"","minutesPacketDocumentIds":[],"minutesPacketEnabled":false,"minutesSectionHeaderDescriptions":null,"minutesSectionHeaderTitles":null,"minutesSnippet":null,"minutesStatus":0,"minutesSummaryDocumentId":"","minutesSummaryDocumentIds":[],"newMeetingDate":null,"newMeetingTime":null,"packetFileSize":89367,"packetFileSizeThreshold":314572800,"recurringId":1955,"recurringType":"NoRepeat","startDateTime":"2026-11-04T06:00:00.000Z","startTime":"05:30 PM","thumbnailOfVideo":"","videoId":"","videoName":null,"videoStatus":""},{"actualEndDate":"2026-11-05 00:00:00.0","actualStartDate":"2026-11-05 00:00:00.0","adjourned":false,"agendaItemAttachmentTitles":[],"agendaItemDescriptions":[],"agendaItemTitles":[],"agendaOCRedContent":"MURRAY CITY PLANNING COMMISSION NOTICE OF MEETING AND AGENDA November 5, 2026 6:30 P.M. MDT Murray City Council Chambers, 10 East 4800 South, Murray, Utah Pre-Meeting: 6:00 p.m. (in the Poplar Room #151 - The public is welcome) The pre-meeting is to briefly review the agenda items and direct questions to staff. The public may view the Murray Planning Commission meeting via live stream at www.murraycitylive.com or https://www.facebook.com/murraycityutah/. You may submit comments via email at pc@murray.utah.gov. Comments are limited to 3 minutes or less. Written comments will be entered into the meeting record. Please include your name and contact information. Supporting materials are available at: https://www.murray.utah.gov/779/Agendas-Attachment. CALL MEETING TO ORDER BUSINESS ITEM(S) 1. Approval of Minutes a. October 1st, 2026 2. Conflict(s) of interest 3. Approval of Findings of Fact a. D.L. Evans Bank EMC - CUP CONDITIONAL USE PERMIT(S)-ADMINISTRATIVE ACTION 4. Tippy Toes Daycare Project #26-095 404 East 4500 South, #A22 Request for a Conditional Use Permit to run a new commercial daycare in the G-O zone. 5. Khang’s Auto Sales 4555 S Commerce Drive, Unit #A300 Request for a Conditional Use Permit for auto sales in the M-G zone. LAND USE TEXT ORDINANCE AMENDMENT(S)-LEGISLATIVE ACTION Project #26-092 6. R-M Zones - Yard Requirements Project #26-091 Proposed text amendments to Sections 17.116.060, 17.120.060, 17.124.060, and 17.128.060. ANNOUNCEMENTS AND QUESTIONS/ADJOURNMENT The next scheduled meeting will be held on November 19, 2026, at 6:30 p.m. MDT in the Murray City Council Chambers, 10 East 4800 South, Murray, Utah. Those wishing to have their comments entered into the record may send an email by 5:00 p.m. the day prior to the meeting date to pc@murray.utah.gov. Comments are limited to three minutes or less (approximately 300 words for emails) and must include your name and address. Special Accommodations for the hearing or visually impaired will be made upon a request to the office of Murray City Recorder (801-264-2662). We would appreciate notification two working days prior to the meeting. TTY is Relay Utah at #711. Committee members may participate in the meeting via telephonic communication. If a Committee member does participate via telephonic communication, the Committee member will be on speakerphone. The speakerphone will be amplified so that the other Committee members and all other persons present will be able to hear all discussions. No agenda item will begin after 10:00 p.m. without a unanimous vote of the Commission. At least 24 hours prior to the meeting, a copy of the foregoing notice was sent to the City Recorder to post in conspicuous view in the front foyer of the Murray City Center, Murray, Utah. A copy of this notice was also posted on Murray City's website www.murray.utah.gov and the state noticing website at http://pmn.utah.gov. ","agendaPacketDocumentId":"DOC621S7769","agendaPacketDocumentIds":["DOC621S7769"],"agendaPacketEnabled":false,"agendaPostedDate":"2026-11-03T17:17:19.000Z","agendaSectionHeaderDescriptions":["<div>The next scheduled meeting will be held on <strong>Thursday, ___________________, at 6:30 p.m. MST in the Murray City Council Chambers, 10 East 4800 South,  Murray, Utah. </strong><br><br></div><div>Those wishing to have their comments read into the record may send an email by 5:00 p.m. the day prior to the meeting date to planningcommission@murray.utah.gov. Comments are limited to three minutes or less (approximately 300 words for emails) and must include your name and address.</div><div><br></div><div>Supporting materials are available on Murray City's website at www.murray.utah.gov.<br><br>Special Accommodations for the hearing or visually impaired will be made upon a request to the office of Murray City Recorder (801-264-2662). We would appreciate notification two working days prior to the meeting. TTY is Relay Utah at #711.<br><br>Committee members may participate in the meeting via telephonic communication. If a Committee member does participate via telephonic communication, the Committee member will be on speakerphone.  The speakerphone will be amplified so that the other Committee members and all other persons present will be able to hear all discussions.<br><br><span style=\"color: rgb(65, 65, 65);\">No agenda item will begin after 10:00 p.m. without a unanimous vote of the Commission.</span> <br><br>At least 24 hours prior to the meeting, a copy of the foregoing notice was sent to the City Recorder to post in conspicuous view in the front foyer of the Murray City Center, Murray, Utah. A copy of this notice was also posted on Murray City's internet website www.murray.utah.gov and the state noticing website at http://pmn.utah.gov.</div>"],"agendaSectionHeaderTitles":["CALL MEETING TO ORDER","BUSINESS ITEM(S)","MAJOR HOME OCCUPATION REVIEW - Administrative Action","CONDITIONAL USE PERMIT(S) - Administrative Action","SITE PLAN REVIEW - Administrative Action","DESIGN REVIEW - Administrative Action","SUBDIVISION REVIEW(S) - Administrative Action","GENERAL PLAN / ZONE MAP AMENDMENT","LAND USE TEXT ORDINANCE AMENDMENT(S)","DISCUSSION ITEM(S)","ANNOUNCEMENTS AND QUESTIONS","ADJOURNMENT"],"agendaSnippet":null,"agendaStatus":5,"agendaSummaryDocumentId":"","agen